func ValidatePayload(st state.BeaconState, payload interfaces.ExecutionData) error {
	random, err := helpers.RandaoMix(st, time.CurrentEpoch(st))
	if err != nil {
		return err
	}
	if !bytes.Equal(payload.PrevRandao(), random) {
		return ErrInvalidPayloadPrevRandao
	}
	t, err := slots.StartTime(st.GenesisTime(), st.Slot())
	if err != nil {
		return err
	}
	if payload.Timestamp() != uint64(t.Unix()) {
		return ErrInvalidPayloadTimeStamp
	}
	return nil
}

ANALYSIS CONTEXT:
- Target: Prysm (Go beacon client) - OffchainLabs fork, commit 238d5c07df
- The checklist properties reference Python EL trie internals (_prepare_trie, encode_node, get_storage_root, EMPTY_TRIE_ROOT) which do NOT exist in the Prysm Go codebase
- Prysm is a consensus layer (CL) client - it does NOT implement the EL state trie directly
- State root validation in Prysm: the state_root field in execution payload is passed through from the EL; Prysm does NOT independently compute or verify the EL state root - it delegates this entirely to the execution engine via NewPayload
- The execution.go StateRoot() method just returns e.p.StateRoot (raw bytes, no validation)
- ProcessPayload validates timestamp, randao, parent hash but NOT state root byte length or encoding
- notifyNewPayload sends payload to EL via engine API; does NOT validate state_root internally
